We have derived improved differentiability properties for solutions to a non-autonomous obstacle problem, formulated as
  \begin{equation*}
  \min\left\{\int_\Omega f\left(x,t,u,D_\theta u\right)dt+\sum_{k=1}^m\mathcal{A}_k\left(\theta,u\right)\;\Big|\;\mathcal{A}_k\left(\cdot,\zeta\right)\geq \mathcal{A}_k\left(\cdot,\omega_k\right)\;\;\mbox{\rm a.e. in }\Omega\;\;\mbox{\rm and}\;\;u\geq \omega_k\;\;\mbox{\rm a.e. in }\Omega_k\;\;\mbox{\rm and}\;\;k=1,\ldots,m\}
  \end{equation*}
  where $\mathcal{A}_1,\ldots,\mathcal{A}_m$ represent elliptic operators with $p$-growth and $p>1$, and $f$ exhibits subquadratic growth, specifically $f(x,t,\zeta,\xi)\leq \left(1+|\xi|^{p}\right)\vartheta(x)\varphi(t)$, under the assumption that the coefficients are Vanishing Mean Oscillation functions. It is worth noting that our results hold true for a broader class of operators
